#!/usr/bin/env ssc
---
name: std-aggregator-approx
version: 1.0.0
description: HyperLogLog, Count-Min Sketch, and T-Digest — approximate aggregators as monoids
---

# Approximate aggregators — sketches as monoids

Exact distinct-count, exact quantiles, and exact top-K cannot be computed in bounded memory over
unbounded data. HyperLogLog, Count-Min Sketch, and T-Digest are probabilistic sketches that ARE
monoids, trading exactness for a known, bounded error at fixed memory. See
[`std/aggregator.ssc`](../std/aggregator.ssc) and
[`specs/aggregation-algebra.md`](../specs/aggregation-algebra.md) §6 for the design.

[Aggregator, runAggregator, strHash, HLLAgg, CMSMonoid, TDigestMonoid](std/aggregator.ssc)

```scalascript
// HyperLogLog: approximate distinct count, usable as an ordinary Aggregator.
val hll  = HLLAgg[String](12, s => strHash(17, s))
val keys = (1 to 10000).toList.map(i => "item-" + i.toString)
println(runAggregator(keys, hll))
println(hll.errorBound)

// merging two overlapping partial sketches gives the correct UNION cardinality
var partA = hll.monoid.empty
for k <- (1 to 3000).toList.map(i => "merge-" + i.toString) do partA = hll.monoid.combine(partA, hll.prepare(k))
var partB = hll.monoid.empty
for k <- (2500 to 6000).toList.map(i => "merge-" + i.toString) do partB = hll.monoid.combine(partB, hll.prepare(k))
println(hll.present(hll.monoid.combine(partA, partB)))

// Count-Min Sketch: approximate frequency, kept as a Monoid plus add/estimate (present needs the
// key as an argument, so it stays outside the plain Aggregator shape - see std/aggregator.ssc).
val cms = CMSMonoid(4, 64)
var cacc = cms.empty
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "apple")
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "apple")
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "apple")
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "banana")
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "banana")
cacc = cms.add(cacc, "cherry")
println(cms.estimate(cacc, "apple"))
println(cms.estimate(cacc, "banana"))
println(cms.estimate(cacc, "cherry"))
println(cms.estimate(cacc, "durian"))

// T-Digest: approximate quantiles, same Monoid-plus-methods shape as Count-Min Sketch.
val td = TDigestMonoid(20)
var d1 = td.empty
for i <- 1 to 100 do d1 = td.addPoint(d1, i.toDouble)
var d2 = td.empty
for i <- 101 to 200 do d2 = td.addPoint(d2, i.toDouble)
val combined = td.combine(d1, d2)
println(combined.centroids.length)
println(td.quantile(combined, 0.5))
println(td.quantile(combined, 0.99))
```
